1. **Chaorong Li, Xiaona Zhang, Zexian Cao.** “Triangular and Fibonacci Number Patterns Driven by Stress on Core/Shell Microstructures.” *Science* **309**, 909–911 (2005). DOI [10.1126/science.1113412](https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1113412). Publisher-deposited abstract and bibliographic record read via Crossref; full publisher page returned 403. The abstract reports geometry-dependent patterns and the authors' strain-energy interpretation, not a mathematical proof.
2. **Chaorong Li, Ailing Ji, Zexian Cao.** “Stressed Fibonacci spiral patterns of definite chirality.” *Applied Physics Letters* **90**, 164102 (2007). DOI [10.1063/1.2728578](https://doi.org/10.1063/1.2728578). Publisher-deposited abstract read. Reports the 3x5 to 13x21 range, conical support, definite chirality, and the least-energy interpretation.
3. **Hyun-Woo Lee, Leonid S. Levitov.** “Universality in Phyllotaxis: a Mechanical Theory.” Chapter in *Symmetry in Plants*, World Scientific (1998), posted as [arXiv:2101.02652](https://arxiv.org/abs/2101.02652) (2021). [Full text](https://arxiv.org/html/2101.02652). Introduction and Sections II.1–II.2 read, including the explicit non-global-minimum qualification. This is the strongest directly relevant warning against conflating energetic evolution with global minimization.
4. **L. S. Levitov.** “Energetic Approach to Phyllotaxis.” *Europhysics Letters* **14**, 533–539 (1991). DOI [10.1209/0295-5075/14/6/006](https://doi.org/10.1209/0295-5075/14/6/006). Metadata read; its role is described in the primary retrospective [3]. Distinct from his “Phyllotaxis of flux lattices in layered superconductors,” *Physical Review Letters* **66**, 224 (1991), DOI [10.1103/PhysRevLett.66.224](https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.66.224).
5. **Pau Atela, Christophe Golé, Scott Hotton.** “A Dynamical System for Plant Pattern Formation: A Rigorous Analysis.” *Journal of Nonlinear Science* **12**(6), 641–676 (volume year 2002; DOI publication metadata and institutional repository date January 2003). DOI [10.1007/s00332-002-0513-1](https://doi.org/10.1007/s00332-002-0513-1); [institutional abstract/manuscript entry](https://scholarworks.smith.edu/mth_facpubs/80/). Author abstract read: fixed points, stability, and bifurcations are the announced rigorous objects.
6. **Adil Mughal, Denis Weaire.** “Theory of cylindrical dense packings of disks.” *Physical Review E* **89**, 042307 (2014). DOI [10.1103/PhysRevE.89.042307](https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevE.89.042307). Metadata checked; commensurate-packing discussion and formulas also read in primary source [13], Appendix C. No uninspected theorem from this article is used in our proofs.
