    42	## 3. Chirality status and the exact remaining gap
    43	
    44	C2 requires distinguishing **relative parastichy chirality** (which of the two spiral families has more members) from the **ontogenetic/generative spiral** (the temporal insertion sequence). These signs can differ and can change for different reasons.
    45	
    46	- The 2007 experiment [2] demonstrates definite chirality under its fabrication conditions, but its abstract does not establish a theorem of disk-size-driven alternation.
    47	- Classical and modern stacking/local-lattice models [3,8–11] provide mechanisms for consecutive parastichy transitions. RESULTS.md derives explicit thresholds and alternation in a frozen golden-angle linearization, rather than assuming the qualitative mechanism solves C2.
    48	- A 2025-online/2026-issue fossil-cone study [17] reports associations between ontogenetic chirality and seed number. The primary abstract describes an observational morphometric study, not a controlled disk-size experiment; it cannot establish the proposed causal alternation law.
    49	- The 2026 Keller–Segel paper [18] reproduces Fibonacci and alternating patterns through growth and signaling instabilities. Its “alternating patterns” are not, by that phrase alone, proof of the book's chirality alternation.
    50	- In an achiral domain with a reflection-invariant energy, opposite chiral minimizers have equal energy at every disk size. That symmetry rules out energetic selection of a unique absolute sign without a symmetry-breaking ingredient, but does not rule out path-dependent branch alternation.
    51	
    52	The unresolved obligation is therefore concrete: fix an apex-directed accretion/relaxation rule, a boundary or seed that fixes the external length scale and any chirality bias, and a robust contact-network count; then prove or certify the parameter intervals and transition sequence. No universal implication “changing size means changing chirality” has been proved here.
    53	
    54	## 4. Primary-source references and reading level
    55	
    56	1. **Chaorong Li, Xiaona Zhang, Zexian Cao.** “Triangular and Fibonacci Number Patterns Driven by Stress on Core/Shell Microstructures.” *Science* **309**, 909–911 (2005). DOI [10.1126/science.1113412](https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1113412). Publisher-deposited abstract and bibliographic record read via Crossref; full publisher page returned 403. The abstract reports geometry-dependent patterns and the authors' strain-energy interpretation, not a mathematical proof.
    57	2. **Chaorong Li, Ailing Ji, Zexian Cao.** “Stressed Fibonacci spiral patterns of definite chirality.” *Applied Physics Letters* **90**, 164102 (2007). DOI [10.1063/1.2728578](https://doi.org/10.1063/1.2728578). Publisher-deposited abstract read. Reports the 3x5 to 13x21 range, conical support, definite chirality, and the least-energy interpretation.
    58	3. **Hyun-Woo Lee, Leonid S. Levitov.** “Universality in Phyllotaxis: a Mechanical Theory.” Chapter in *Symmetry in Plants*, World Scientific (1998), posted as [arXiv:2101.02652](https://arxiv.org/abs/2101.02652) (2021). [Full text](https://arxiv.org/html/2101.02652). Introduction and Sections II.1–II.2 read, including the explicit non-global-minimum qualification. This is the strongest directly relevant warning against conflating energetic evolution with global minimization.
    59	4. **L. S. Levitov.** “Energetic Approach to Phyllotaxis.” *Europhysics Letters* **14**, 533–539 (1991). DOI [10.1209/0295-5075/14/6/006](https://doi.org/10.1209/0295-5075/14/6/006). Metadata read; its role is described in the primary retrospective [3]. Distinct from his “Phyllotaxis of flux lattices in layered superconductors,” *Physical Review Letters* **66**, 224 (1991), DOI [10.1103/PhysRevLett.66.224](https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.66.224).
    60	5. **Pau Atela, Christophe Golé, Scott Hotton.** “A Dynamical System for Plant Pattern Formation: A Rigorous Analysis.” *Journal of Nonlinear Science* **12**(6), 641–676 (volume year 2002; DOI publication metadata and institutional repository date January 2003). DOI [10.1007/s00332-002-0513-1](https://doi.org/10.1007/s00332-002-0513-1); [institutional abstract/manuscript entry](https://scholarworks.smith.edu/mth_facpubs/80/). Author abstract read: fixed points, stability, and bifurcations are the announced rigorous objects.
    61	6. **Adil Mughal, Denis Weaire.** “Theory of cylindrical dense packings of disks.” *Physical Review E* **89**, 042307 (2014). DOI [10.1103/PhysRevE.89.042307](https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevE.89.042307). Metadata checked; commensurate-packing discussion and formulas also read in primary source [13], Appendix C. No uninspected theorem from this article is used in our proofs.
    62	7. **Adil Mughal, Denis Weaire.** “Phyllotaxis, disk packing, and Fibonacci numbers.” *Physical Review E* **95**, 022401 (2017). DOI [10.1103/PhysRevE.95.022401](https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevE.95.022401); [arXiv:1608.05824](https://arxiv.org/abs/1608.05824). Author abstract read. The local principles are dense packing, homogeneity and continuity, not a certificate of the cone's global packing optimum.
    63	8. **Christophe Golé, Jacques Dumais, Stéphane Douady.** “Fibonacci or quasi-symmetric phyllotaxis. Part I: why?” *Acta Societatis Botanicorum Poloniae* (2016), article 3533. DOI [10.5586/asbp.3533](https://doi.org/10.5586/asbp.3533); [institutional author entry](https://scholarworks.smith.edu/mth_facpubs/32/). Primary abstract read; reports both Fibonacci-like and quasi-symmetric solutions of disk accretion. The institutional volume field is not relied upon because it is inconsistent with common bibliographic indexing.
    64	9. **Jonathan Swinton.** “Disk-stacking models are consistent with Fibonacci and non-Fibonacci structure in sunflowers.” [arXiv:2407.05857v2](https://arxiv.org/html/2407.05857v2) (2024), preprint. Full-text Sections 1–5 read, including actual contact-chain parastichy definitions, finite transitions, non-Fibonacci data and parameter selection after inspection. It is cited as a preprint; no unverified journal status or priority assertion is imported.
    65	10. **Roland Bacher.** “On geodesics of phyllotaxis.” *Confluentes Mathematici* **6**(1), 3–27 (2014). DOI [10.5802/cml.10](https://doi.org/10.5802/cml.10); [arXiv:1301.7568](https://arxiv.org/abs/1301.7568); [journal PDF](https://www.numdam.org/item/10.5802/cml.10.pdf). Theorem 1.1, linearization, Sections 6–7 and parastichy transitions read. This is direct prior art for the local geometry and cautions against claiming the reduced transition mechanism as new.
    66	11. **Shigeki Akiyama.** “Spiral Delone sets and three distance theorem.” [arXiv:1904.10815v2](https://arxiv.org/abs/1904.10815) (2019). [Full manuscript](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1904.10815). Theorems 2–3, Diophantine conditions, and stated generalization questions read. The theorem concerns the Delone property, not global maximum density.
    67	12. **H. S. Ansell, A. A. Tomlinson, N. K. Wilkin.** “Transitions between phyllotactic lattice states in curved geometries.” *Scientific Reports* **10**, 17411 (2020). DOI [10.1038/s41598-020-74158-x](https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-020-74158-x); [arXiv:2001.10501v2 full text](https://arxiv.org/html/2001.10501v2); [PubMed record](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/33060641/). Model and Sections 2–4 read: intrinsic `K_0` interaction, fixed-density reservoirs, numerical ground-state methods, and non-Fibonacci states. The HTML rendering's later date is not the publication date.
    68	13. **Jessica H. Sun, Abigail Plummer, Grace H. Zhang, David R. Nelson, Vinothan N. Manoharan.** “Geometric frustration of hard-disk packings on cones.” *Physical Review E* **108**, 054608 (2023). DOI [10.1103/PhysRevE.108.054608](https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevE.108.054608); [arXiv:2309.14446 full manuscript](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2309.14446). Methods, discussion, conclusion and Appendices A/C read. Section II states the special sector angles `60 degrees * P`; their simulations deliberately avoid them. Conclusion explicitly calls for simulations/experiments including kinetics, thermal fluctuations and entropy. Their [public code](https://github.com/manoharan-lab/cone-disk-packings) and [data DOI](https://doi.org/10.7910/DVN/ZQ4BUR) are linked in the paper but were not cloned or reproduced here.
    69	14. **Jessica H. Sun, Grace H. Zhang, Abigail Plummer, Caroline Martin, Nabila Tanjeem, David R. Nelson, Vinothan N. Manoharan.** “Colloidal Crystallization on Cones.” *Physical Review Letters* **134**, 018201 (2025). DOI [10.1103/PhysRevLett.134.018201](https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.134.018201); [primary abstract via PubMed](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/39913697/). Abstract read after publisher/author-page access failed. Grain-boundary and finite-band observations above come from that abstract, not an unverified search summary.
    70	15. **D. P. Hardin, E. B. Saff.** “Minimal Riesz energy point configurations for rectifiable d-dimensional manifolds.” *Advances in Mathematics* **193**, 174–204 (2005). DOI [10.1016/j.aim.2004.05.006](https://doi.org/10.1016/j.aim.2004.05.006); [arXiv:math-ph/0311024](https://arxiv.org/abs/math-ph/0311024). Author abstract read; only its asymptotic distribution statement is used here. No transfer of its assumptions to intrinsic Coulomb energy is asserted.
    71	16. **Hai-Chau Chang, Lih-Chung Wang.** “A Simple Proof of Thue's Theorem on Circle Packing.” [arXiv:1009.4322](https://arxiv.org/abs/1009.4322) (2010), proof exposition of the classical planar theorem. Author abstract read. The planar packing theorem is an explicitly imported mathematical baseline in RESULTS.md, not a locally rediscovered result.
    72	17. **Mariah M. Howell, Ronny Rößler, Carole T. Gee.** “Phyllotaxis, ontogeny and CT imaging: old and new approaches to understanding optimal seed packing in Middle Jurassic Araucaria mirabilis cones.” *Annals of Botany* (online 2025; issue 2026). DOI [10.1093/aob/mcaf325](https://doi.org/10.1093/aob/mcaf325). Publisher-deposited abstract read. It describes 21 analyzed cones; a search summary said 30, so that summary was rejected. No sample-size inference or experimental causal claim is made from it.
    73	18. **Michael F. Staddon.** “Phyllotaxis in a Keller-Segel model.” *Physical Review E* **113**, 034407 (2026). DOI [10.1103/9yk5-b4q2](https://doi.org/10.1103/9yk5-b4q2). Publisher-deposited abstract read: radial growth, signal-source competition, and linear stability analysis. This extends the status check to 2026 but does not settle elastic C1 or disk-size C2.
    74	
    75	### Historical source correction
    76	
    77	The Oklahoma item is accessible: [J. Albert's course project list, Version 3, Summer 2008](https://www.math.ou.edu/~jalbert/courses/projects.pdf), item 15. Its exact characterization is “least-energy configurations of discs (I think) on a cone,” and it points to the 2005/2007 experiments. It is an informal course-project suggestion, not a formal published densest-packing conjecture or proof. The book's summary should not be upgraded into a precise theorem statement.
    78	
    79	### Search and access limitations
    80	
    81	Primary texts were preferred over generated search answers. Search covered the book's titles, cone hard-disk packing, conical crystal ground states, phyllotaxis chirality, Fermat-spiral density, and 2025–2026 developments. Multiple publisher pages returned 403/401; author manuscripts, deposited abstracts, or PubMed were used with the reading level stated above. One search-suggested `preprints.org/manuscript/202608.2110` URL was inaccessible and not independently located by its identifier; it supports no claim. Absence from this bounded review establishes neither nonexistence nor novelty.
    82	
    83	## 5. Research direction after these certificates
    84	
    85	The attainable result is not “Fibonacci is always optimal,” but a precise separation between geometric constraints, kinetic branch selection, and equilibrium. The full target needs a physically grounded energy and a broader contact-topology class. Fixing those assumptions is the single highest-value prerequisite; more random starts in an arbitrary energy landscape would not repair their absence.

